  "_rotationComment": "Every match is different: each land's own table is always used (its weights jittered by tableJitter), plus rotationPicks species (rotationPicksByLand for a land with a smaller pool) drawn from that land's rotation pool for that match, picked by weight without repeats and never one already in the land's table. Every line that can Mega Evolve lives in an ordinary table (Riolu and Ralts in the forest, Charmander as a starter and Gastly in the red wood, Snorunt and Absol in the snow, Larvitar as a pseudo-legendary and Onix on the desert rocks): none is guaranteed in a match any more. Starters and pseudo-legendaries are not in these tables: see rare.",
  "rare": {
    "_comment": "Starter Pokemon and pseudo-legendary families, kept out of the tables above so every member of a group has the same actual availability whatever its land's size or table: each species is placed in a match with probability perMatch (one of it; a perMatch above 1 places floor(perMatch) and one more with the remainder), at a random ordinary spot of its land (its own ground, or a meadow or beach whose nearest land it is), taking that spot from the land's table. Its level is the land's levels + levelsOver plus the usual rise toward the Shadow Crystal, so where it lands decides how strong (and how evolved) it is. Starters keep to their type's land (grass in the forest, fire in the red wood, water in the snow, Mudkip in the desert); pseudo-legendaries to the lands they had. These are ordinary wild spawns: the stronger encounters' pseudo-legendary picks (strong.pseudoChance) are separate.",
    "levelsOver": [
      3,
      2
    ],
